subproblems.statement:
Let P ∈ ℕ and let μ be a measure on the Borel σ-algebra of ℝ^P with μ(K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ ℝ^P. Let Q(x, ρ) be an arbitrary predicate on pairs (x, ρ) ∈ ℝ^P × ℝ. Let W ⊆ ℝ^P be open and let E ⊆ W be an arbitrary set, not necessarily measurable. Assume that for every x ∈ E and every δ > 0 there is ρ with 0 < ρ < δ and Q(x, ρ). Then there are a countable set t ⊆ E and a function r : ℝ^P → ℝ such that:
(a) for every x ∈ t, r(x) > 0, the closed ball B̄_{r(x)}(x) is contained in W, and Q(x, r(x)) holds;
(b) the closed balls B̄_{r(x)}(x), x ∈ t, are pairwise disjoint, i.e. B̄_{r(x)}(x) ∩ B̄_{r(y)}(y) = ∅ for distinct x, y ∈ t;
(c) μ(E ∖ ⋃_{x∈t} B̄_{r(x)}(x)) = 0, where μ is the outer measure.

Let P ∈ ℕ, let μ be a measure on the Borel σ-algebra of ℝ^P, and let g : ℝ^P → ℝ and θ ∈ ℝ. Let t ⊆ ℝ^P be a countable set and B : ℝ^P → 𝒫(ℝ^P) a family of sets, and put V := ⋃_{x∈t} B(x). Assume:
- B(x) is measurable for every x ∈ t;
- the sets B(x), x ∈ t, are pairwise disjoint, i.e. B(x) ∩ B(y) = ∅ for distinct x, y ∈ t;
- μ(V) < ∞;
- g is μ-integrable on V.
If ∫_{B(x)} g dμ ≤ θ·μ(B(x)) for every x ∈ t, then ∫_V g dμ ≤ θ·μ(V). All measures are read as real numbers via ENNReal.toReal.
